{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011tGtdgfb8UKepi3dFxdMsC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. This project derives specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go binaries), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets, scaffolded externally), `docs/` (human-authored specs).\n\n**Current state:** `pkg/sys/` and `pkg/testutils/` have source code on the working branch (confirmed by source_code). `pkg/format/` has specs complete but no code. No `cmd/` utilities have code on this branch. `magefiles/` is scaffolded infrastructure (DD7 excludes it from generation).\n\n**Current release:** rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Within rel00.0: uc003-sys and uc004-testutils are effectively done (source code exists); uc001-magefiles is excluded from generation (DD7); **uc002-format is the remaining task** — specs complete, code not started.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nPer P1 (release-driven priority), rel00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Within it, `pkg/format/` is the only remaining generation target. Per P5/P8, libraries before consumers — format must exist before its consumers (wc for column alignment in rel01.0, du for human-readable sizes in rel01.3). ANSI colors are deferred since their consumer (ls) is in rel99.0. The task covers human-readable size formatting and column alignment — the two capabilities needed by current-scope releases.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format/ human-readable size formatting and column alignment (rel00.0-uc002-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format/ component -- responsibility, capabilities, and design decisions)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the format package PRD -- search for a file matching prd*format*.yaml; read all requirements and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (format use case)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test suite for release 00.0 -- format section)\n      - pkg/sys/doc.go (reference pattern for doc.go copyright header and package comment style)\n      - pkg/sys/stat.go (reference pattern for exported types, GoDoc comments, and file structure)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (reference pattern for naming the primary source file after the primary exported type, not after the package name)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/doc.go\n        action: create\n        note: Package documentation with copyright header and PRD requirement references\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable size formatting -- bytes to K/M/G/T/P/E with IEC and SI unit systems\n      - path: pkg/format/columns.go\n        action: create\n        note: Column alignment for tabular output -- right-aligned numeric columns, left-aligned text columns\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement human-readable size formatting that converts byte counts to\n          human-readable strings matching GNU coreutils --human-readable output format.\n          Support both 1024-based (IEC) and 1000-based (SI) unit systems. The exact\n          function signatures, unit suffixes, rounding rules, and edge-case behavior\n          (zero bytes, negative values, exact multiples) must follow the format PRD.\n          Read the PRD before implementing.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement column alignment for tabular output. Support right-aligned\n          numeric columns and left-aligned text columns for multi-row data. Accept\n          a representation of rows and columns and produce formatted output with\n          consistent column widths. This capability is used by wc (right-aligned\n          counts) and du (right-aligned sizes with left-aligned paths). Follow the\n          format PRD for the exact API.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Create doc.go with package documentation following the pattern in\n          pkg/sys/doc.go. Include the copyright header, SPDX license identifier,\n          a doc comment describing the package purpose and listing implemented\n          PRD requirement IDs, and the package declaration.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          All exported functions and types must have GoDoc comments. Use only the\n          Go standard library -- no external dependencies beyond what is already\n          in go.mod. Follow the project file naming convention: name each source\n          file after its primary exported functionality (e.g., size.go for size\n          formatting, columns.go for column alignment), not after the package name.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Follow the copyright header pattern from pkg/sys/doc.go verbatim:\n          line 1 is \"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\"\n          and line 2 is \"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\". A blank line separates\n          the copyright from the package doc comment.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          pkg/format/ uses only the Go standard library (fmt, strings, math,\n          strconv as needed). It does NOT depend on golang.org/x/sys or any other\n          external module. This is per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology choices which\n          list golang.org/x/sys as the only external dependency, scoped to pkg/sys/.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          ANSI color output is NOT in scope for this task. Only implement\n          human-readable size formatting (R1) and column alignment (R2). Color\n          support is an ARCHITECTURE.yaml capability for pkg/format/ but its\n          primary consumer (ls) is deferred to rel99.0. It will be added in a\n          separate task when needed.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: pkg/format/doc.go exists with copyright header, SPDX identifier, package doc comment referencing PRD requirement IDs, and package declaration\n      - id: AC2\n        text: pkg/format/size.go exports at least one function that formats byte counts as human-readable strings with unit suffixes, supporting both IEC (1024-based) and SI (1000-based) modes\n      - id: AC3\n        text: pkg/format/columns.go exports at least one function that produces column-aligned tabular output with right-aligned numeric fields and consistent column widths\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/format/ succeeds with no compilation errors\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/format/ reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26551,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26551},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4368ce4b-4c76-4001-b6b3-8cdb04ed041d","uuid":"2febaaff-7c0c-4865-aa08-08561e7295a6"}
